{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299053-a-flavor-of-falconry","id":1299053,"title":"A Flavor of Falconry","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-23T15:38:22-07:00","id":1299053,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon6.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> A Flavor of Falconry","content":"I don't know how well known this Fighting Merit is, but I would like to shine a small spotlight on Falconry Style (Fighting Merit) out of the Hunter book <b>Hurt Locker</b>. I was wondering around on YouTube two years ago and I saw a video on Asian peoples using these giant Steppe Eagles to hunt <i>wolves</i> of all things. Now that I remembered this, I can strongly recommend this Fighting Merit for PCs or antagonists who will encounter Uratha. However using an eagle to hunt IR requires a lengthy process including several years of apprenticeships using smaller birds of prey. A character using this Fighting Merit ought to heavily invested in their boid if they want their PC to feel realistic. Now on the actual use of this merit in combat, using a large bird of prey to after Uratha needs to done tactically by having the magnificent bird go after the Uratha when he or she is in these several forms: <i>Hishu, Dalu, and Durhan</i>. The more wolven forms are too dangerous IMO to attack directly, but you could use the Flyby (\u2022\u2022) command to distract the doggo in a fight (especially if they are not Death Raging). I hope the information I have given is accurate, helpful, and fun. Good day (or night) to you all!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}